{
  // Dependency-vulnerability gate for CI (replaces the bare `npm audit --audit-level=high`,
  // which has no way to record a reasoned exception).
  //
  // The gate stays sharp: anything high/critical that is NOT listed below fails the build.
  // `allowlist` is per-advisory (GHSA id), never per-severity — we do not lower the level.
  //
  // Adding an entry requires, in this file: (1) the advisory id, (2) why it does not apply to
  // THIS codebase, measured — not assumed, (3) an expiry date, (4) what removes the need for it.
  // An expired entry is a task, not a renewal: re-check it, do not extend it by reflex.
  //
  // Take the fix first. Of the four high advisories open against this tree on 2026-07-29, two
  // were closed by a version bump (postcss 8.5.24, react-router-dom 7.18.1) and the two below
  // had no adoptable fix. Policy: docs/development/dependency-audit.md
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "moderate": false,
  "high": true,
  "critical": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg — brace-expansion "DoS via unbounded expansion length causing an
    // out-of-memory process crash" (high). The advisory declares ONE range, `<= 5.0.7`, with
    // `first_patched_version = 5.0.8` (checked against the GitHub advisory API, not inferred):
    // there is no patched 1.x and no patched 2.x. Every brace-expansion below 5.0.8 is affected
    // forever.
    //
    // Why we cannot simply take 5.0.8 everywhere (measured 2026-07-29 on this tree): the two
    // remaining old instances are pulled by `minimatch@3.1.5` (via eslint-plugin-import /
    // eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y, which pin `minimatch@^3.1.2`) and `minimatch@5.1.9` (via
    // openapi-typescript → @redocly/openapi-core). minimatch 3.x/5.x consume brace-expansion
    // through its **old CommonJS default-function export**, which 5.x no longer provides.
    // Forcing a flat `"brace-expansion": "^5.0.8"` override installs cleanly and then crashes
    // the lint step at runtime with `TypeError: expand is not a function`
    // (minimatch/minimatch.js:271, via @eslint/config-array). Verified by doing it. So the
    // overrides pin per major line: 1.1.16 / ^2.1.3 / ^5.0.8 — the newest of each — and the
    // 1.x and 2.x instances stay inside the advisory with nowhere to go.
    //
    // Why the residual risk is acceptable here: brace-expansion is **dev-only in this repo**.
    // `npm ls --omit=dev --all` contains zero brace-expansion and zero minimatch nodes, so it
    // is absent from the shipped `public_html/admin` bundle. The only consumers are the lint
    // toolchain and the OpenAPI codegen, and the glob patterns they expand come from our own
    // config files — not from user input, a request, or a report payload. The DoS has no
    // reachable attacker-controlled path.
    //
    // Expiry: 2026-08-31. Removed by moving both consumers off minimatch 3.x/5.x — an eslint
    // 10 upgrade (its @eslint/config-array 0.23.x takes minimatch ^10, which takes
    // brace-expansion ^5.0.5) together with an eslint-plugin-import / eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y /
    // @redocly/openapi-core bump. That is a toolchain wave, deliberately not bundled into this
    // security PR. Re-argue at expiry; do not extend by reflex.
    "GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg",

    // GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before
    // 400 Response" (high). Vulnerable range 7.12.0–8.2.0; there is NO fix in the 7.x line
    // (react-router-dom stops at 7.18.1; the fix is react-router v8 >= 8.3.0, a different
    // package and a breaking upgrade).
    //
    // Why it does not apply here (measured 2026-07-29 on this tree):
    //   - `src/app/router.tsx` builds the whole route table with `createBrowserRouter` and
    //     **element-only** route objects. A grep for route-level `action:` / `loader:` keys
    //     across `src/` returns 0 hits, so there is no route action for a server to execute.
    //   - All 17 react-router call sites import from `react-router-dom` (the client package).
    //     `@react-router/dev`, `react-router/rsc`, `createStaticHandler` and
    //     `StaticRouterProvider` appear 0 times in `src/` and in `package.json` — no RSC mode,
    //     no server components, no framework-mode server runtime.
    //   - `vite.config.ts` builds to `outDir: ../public_html/admin` — a **static SPA bundle**
    //     served as files. There is no server that could run a route action before returning 400.
    // The advisory's attack path has no counterpart in a client-only bundle.
    //
    // Expiry: 2026-08-31. Removed by the react-router v8 migration wave (bundled with the
    // NENE2 RR8 re-evaluation). If that wave slips past the expiry, the entry must be
    // re-argued in a PR — not silently extended.
    "GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2",
  ],
}
